  "query_preview": "..\nA convergence zone between the monsoon westerlies and east trade\nwinds is setting up right over the Marianas tonight as widespread \nshowers and isolated thunderstorms are now expected over Guam with a \npotential for locally heavy rainfall. Precipitation chances will\ndecrease north of Guam, remaining scattered over Tinian and Saipan.\nThe convergence zone is expected to move out of the area by tomorrow\nmorning and be replaced with scattered showers and isolated\nthunderstorms. Lower cloud coverage and light winds over Tinian and\nSaipan could allow for island effect showers and thunderstorms over \nthe southern portion of Saipan. Light and variable winds Tuesday\nmorning will allow for island effect showers and thunderstorms to \ndevelop over Guam, Tinian, and Saipan, likely pushing south as a\nnorth wind begins to move into the area. Depending on the track and\nintensity of Invest 92W, another convergence zone may develop Tuesday\nnight. Afterwards, scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms are\nexpected most days for the rest of the forecast period. However, a\nfair amount of uncertainty remains due to 92W.",
